##  Documented machine's IP address, subnet, gateway, DNS servers, and MAC address using ip and resolv.conf

> **Timestamp:** `2026-06-30 19:50:24`

### 01. `ip -brief addr show`

```bash
ip -brief addr show
```

**Output:**

```text
lo               UNKNOWN        127.0.0.1/8 ::1/128 
eth0             UP             172.30.22.244/20 fe80::215:5dff:fec8:6bb7/64 
```

### 02. `ip route | grep default`

```bash
ip route | grep default
```

**Output:**

```text
default via 172.30.16.1 dev eth0 proto kernel 
```

### 03. `cat /etc/resolv.config`

```bash
cat /etc/resolv.config
```

**Output:**

```text
cat: /etc/resolv.config: No such file or directory
```

### 04. `ip -brief link show`

```bash
ip -brief link show
```

**Output:**

```text
lo               UNKNOWN        00:00:00:00:00:00 <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> 
eth0             UP             00:15:5d:c8:6b:b7 <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> 
```

